# The weather card is re-rendered hourly and is stale within the hour, so the
# render itself is build output, not a record worth keeping. Committing it
# added ~1GB of permanent git objects a year. The queued copy under
# Utilities/uploads_queue/ is what actually reaches Drive.
Utilities/Weather Ad/weather-at-a-glance.png
Utilities/Weather Ad/weather-at-a-glance.html

# Same as the weather card: rebuilt hourly and uploaded straight to Drive, so
# the render is build output rather than anything worth keeping in history.
Utilities/Service Ad/service-ad.png
Utilities/Service Ad/service-ad.html

# The newsletter card now carries the week's actual items and is re-rendered
# hourly, so the render is build output like the weather and service cards.
# newsletter_ad_state.json (the Gemini cache) is what's worth keeping.
Utilities/Newsletter Ad/newsletter-ad.png
Utilities/Newsletter Ad/newsletter-ad.html
